      "pages": [42],
      "taughtInClass": false,
      "tip": "The imperative is the shortest form of the verb (the root): tal! The infinitive adds -e (at tale), but not after a vowel (at bo, at gå). The present adds -(e)r: taler.\nExample: tal / at tale / taler = speak.",
      "items": [
